---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
requires:
  - predators
  - regeneration
description: Animation - the figures of the deep move, and every event of a run is seen as it happens.
---

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: draws every animation of a :Run: in `src/game/render/`, timed by the simulation's `tick`, so animations stand still whenever `tick` does; no animation changes the simulation state, a collision circle or a timing.

- The simulation keeps a list of the events animations are drawn for - a :GeneFragment: collected, a :PlanktonCloud: used, one of the :Hearts: lost, a :Predator: purified, a :Rift: opened, a :Level: started - each with its kind, position, the figure it concerns and its `tick`, and drops each one 1 s after it happened; the list is not part of :StateSnapshot:.

- The twinkle of each :PlanktonCloud: speck is timed by a hash of the cloud's index, the speck's index and `tick`, never by the :RunSeed: generator.

- The shimmer band of :CombJelly:, :FlickerJelly: and :SplitJelly: is drawn with the canvas `lighter` composite operation.

- :Implementation: draws the :Jellyfish: tentacles as canvas strokes, so `src/game/art/jellyfish.svg` holds only its bell and core.

- :Implementation: draws the moving background of :TitleScreen: and :RegenerationScreen: on a canvas behind the page content, timed by `requestAnimationFrame`, apart from the game loop.

- :Implementation: bundles the Nunito font through the `@fontsource/nunito` npm package, weights 400, 600 and 800, imported once in `src/main.tsx`, never from a network font service.
  - The canvas draws a :Run:'s first frame only after `document.fonts.load` of Nunito resolves.
  - Every `ctx.font` names `Nunito` first, with `sans-serif` as the fallback.

- :Implementation: sets every colour of `src/game/palette.ts` that the pages use as a CSS custom property on the document root once at startup, so every page and overlay, :PauseMenu: and :RegenerationScreen: included, reads the same variables.

- :Implementation: runs served from any base path, such as `/turritopsis-undying-tide/` on GitHub Pages.
  - Vite's `base` is read from the `BASE_PATH` environment variable at build time, `/` when it is unset.
  - The router's `basename` is `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, and every link, navigation and asset URL is relative to it.
  - `npm run build` also writes `dist/404.html`, a copy of `dist/index.html`, so reloading `/dive` or `/scoreboard` under the base path opens the game.

- :Implementation: draws the icon of each :Upgrade: kind from its own SVG file, `src/game/art/upgrade-<id>.svg`, used both on the :UpgradeChoice: and in :Hud:.

***functional specs***

- The :Jellyfish: figure pulses: its bell narrows to 90% of its width and lengthens to 110% of its height, then relaxes back to its drawn size, once every 1.2 s, and once every 0.8 s while Arrow Up, W, Arrow Down or S is held.
  - Up and Down held together count as neither held.
  - While Up or Down is held, each contraction starts with a stroke of the :Jellyfish:; a stroke that starts mid-pulse takes the bell into its contraction from where it stands, without a jump.
  - The figure pulses about its centre; the :Jellyfish: circle stays radius 24.

- The :Jellyfish: has 8 wavy tentacles in the palette's player tentacles colour, hanging from the lower rim of its bell, spread evenly along it, each moving on its own.
  - From left to right they are 54, 60, 64, 68, 66, 62, 58 and 52 px long, sway once every 3.0, 3.6, 4.1, 3.3, 3.9, 4.4, 3.5 and 3.8 s, and start 0, 0.55, 0.3, 0.8, 0.15, 0.65, 0.4 and 0.9 of a cycle into their sway.
  - Each sway is a wave running from the rim to the tip: 0 px across at the rim, growing to 9, 11, 8, 10, 12, 9, 11 and 10 px at the tip, the tip a whole cycle behind the rim, so each tentacle holds one full wave along its length.
  - Each contraction of the bell's pulse draws every tip up to 4 px in towards the bell's centre line, and they spread back as the bell relaxes.
  - A tentacle is a smooth curve through at least 8 points, tapering from 3 px wide at the rim to 1 px at the tip.
  - Its bend follows a change of the :Jellyfish: velocity with a lag growing along it, reaching the tip 0.8 s after the rim, so the tips keep drifting the old way after it turns or stops.
  - At rest they hang straight out of the lower rim, away from the bell's top; while it moves they bend from that line to stream out opposite its velocity, more the faster it moves, fully behind it at 240 px/s and above.
  - When it stops, they swing back to hanging straight out of the lower rim over 1.5 s, easing out, never in one step.
  - They are drawn beneath the bell, the 4 inner ones over the 4 outer ones.

- The :Jellyfish: bell is drawn turned to its :Heading:, its top facing along it, turning as its :Heading: turns and holding its angle while it does not.
  - The bell's pulse, its core and every mark drawn on it turn with it, and the tentacles hang from its lower rim as turned, keeping their sway, lag and streaming opposite the velocity.
  - The line the tentacles hang along at rest, and bend from while it moves, turns with the bell: it runs out of the lower rim away from the bell's top as turned, never towards the bottom of the screen while the bell is turned, so no tentacle crosses the bell.
  - Once it has stopped, the tentacles swing back to that line as the bell holds its angle, hanging straight down only when the bell is upright.
  - The bell is drawn at the :Heading: alone: the :Jellyfish: circle stays as it is, and the tentacles at rest hang straight out opposite the :Heading:.

- Every :CombJelly:, :FlickerJelly: and :SplitJelly: shimmers: a band of light a quarter of its diameter tall sweeps down its figure from top to bottom once every 0.8 s, clipped to its circle.
  - The band is the palette's comb-jelly colour at 60% opacity, added to the figure's colours so it brightens them.
  - Each one starts its sweep at a point of the cycle drawn from its `id`, so no two are in step.

- A :SplitJelly: figure swells to 105% of its drawn size and back once every 1 s, about its centre.
  - Its circle stays radius 26.

- Each anchovy of an :AnchovySchool: flicks its tail: its figure turns 10° to either side of its heading and back, 4 times a second, about its head.
  - The anchovies of a school flick out of step, each one an eighth of the cycle behind the one before it.
  - The figure faces the way the :AnchovySchool: sweeps.

- An :ArrowWorm: wriggles while it lunges: its figure, faced along the lunge, is drawn in 4 strips from head to tail, each shifted sideways by a wave of 3 px that runs from head to tail 5 times a second.
  - In every other phase it is drawn straight, its quiver while aiming unchanged.
  - Its circle stays radius 14.

- A :StingingJelly: bell pulses, narrowing to 90% of its width and lengthening to 110% of its height and back once every 1.0 s, and its tentacle segments sway.
  - Each segment is drawn shifted up to 4 px across the line of the tentacles, in a wave that runs from the bell to the last segment once every 1.5 s.
  - Its bell and segment circles stay where they are, and their radii unchanged.

- Each :GeneFragment: not yet collected bobs and glows: its figure is drawn up to 3 px above and below its position, once every 2 s, inside a halo of radius 20 in the palette's gene-fragment colour whose opacity rises from 30% to 70% and falls back on the same cycle.
  - Each :GeneFragment: of a :Level: is a sixth of the cycle behind the one before it.
  - Its circle stays at its position, radius 12.

- Each :PlanktonCloud: not yet used drifts and twinkles: its figure is drawn moving round a circle of 4 px about its position once every 5 s, with 6 specks of radius 1.5 px in the palette's plankton colour inside its circle.
  - Each speck lights up and fades out over 0.4 s, at moments that look random, at least once every 2 s.
  - The same `tick` always draws the same specks, and the twinkle changes no :RunSeed: draw.
  - Its circle stays at its position, radius 30.

- The :Rift: figure swirls about its centre: one turn every 8 s while closed, one turn every 2 s while open.
  - An open :Rift: has a halo of radius 56 in the palette's open-rift colour, its opacity rising from 30% to 60% and back once every 1.2 s.
  - When the :Rift: opens, its figure grows from 60% to its full size over 0.6 s, and a ring in the open-rift colour widens from 40 px to 80 px and fades out over the same 0.6 s.
  - Its circle stays radius 40, and it can be entered from the tick it opens.

- Collecting a :GeneFragment: or using up a :PlanktonCloud: shows a burst where it lay.
  - A :GeneFragment: throws out 8 sparks of radius 2 px in the palette's gene-fragment colour, evenly spread, flying 30 px out and fading over 0.4 s.
  - A :PlanktonCloud: throws out 10 specks of radius 1.5 px in the palette's plankton colour, evenly spread, flying 40 px out and fading over 0.5 s.

- Losing one of the :Hearts: shows the loss: the heart going from :Hud: grows to 150% and fades out over 0.5 s where it stood, and a ring in the palette's heart colour widens from 24 px to 48 px around the :Jellyfish: and fades out over 0.3 s.
  - The :Invulnerability: blink is unchanged.

- A purified :Predator: dissolves: its figure stays drawn where it was purified, growing to 130% of its size and fading out over 0.5 s, while 6 specks in the palette's sting colour rise 20 px from it and fade.
  - A purified :StingingJelly: dissolves with its tentacle segments, each growing to 130% about its own centre and fading out with the bell.
  - Each anchovy of a purified :AnchovySchool: dissolves where it was.
  - A dissolving figure cannot touch the :Jellyfish: and is not in :StateSnapshot:.
  - A :SplitJelly: that splits does not dissolve.

- Each :Level: after the first is dived into: for 0.8 s from its start it is drawn shifted 120 px down, rising to its place, under the palette's darkness overlay fading from fully opaque to clear.
  - :Hud: is drawn above it, unshifted.
  - The :Level: plays as usual during the 0.8 s.

- :TitleScreen: and :RegenerationScreen: have a drifting background: 12 motes of radius 2 to 5 px in the palette's bell colour at 25% opacity rise at 15 to 30 px/s, swaying up to 10 px to either side of their line, and come back in at the bottom after leaving at the top.
  - :TitleScreen: draws them over the sunlit water gradient of the palette.
  - :RegenerationScreen: draws them over the :Level: as it stood at the :RunEnd:.
  - Their sizes, speeds and starting places are the same every time the screen opens.

- The :Jellyfish: shrinks into its :Polyp: and unfurls out of it: over the first 0.4 s of the :Polyp: stage, the :Jellyfish: figure, tentacles with it, shrinks to 40% and fades out while the polyp figure grows from 40% to its full size and fades in; over the last 0.4 s the same is played backwards.
  - Both figures scale about the :Jellyfish: centre.
  - Between the two, only the polyp figure is drawn, at its full size but for its pulse.
  - The :Jellyfish: does not pulse while it is a :Polyp:.
  - The polyp figure pulses while a :Polyp:, from the end of its growing until its shrinking starts: it swells to 112% of its full size and back once every 0.8 s, about the :Jellyfish: centre, inside a halo of radius 36 in the palette's player core colour whose opacity rises from 15% to 45% and falls back on the same cycle.
  - The :Polyp: circle stays radius 24 throughout.
  - The polyp figure has no sharp corners: its stalk is a rounded column, its top end hidden under the bell and its foot a rounded base, and every outline of the figure is a smooth curve.

- Every text of the game - on :TitleScreen:, :PauseMenu:, :RegenerationScreen:, the scoreboard page at `/scoreboard`, :DivePage: and in :Hud: - is set in Nunito, with `sans-serif` as the fallback.
  - Headings are weight 800, buttons and :Hud: labels 600, every other text 400.
  - Every heading, label and button text is in the palette's HUD text colour, secondary text in its HUD text-secondary colour; none is in the browser's default black.
  - Secondary text is the controls list of :TitleScreen:, the notes of the scoreboard page, and the line under the :RunEnd: reason heading.
  - :PauseMenu: and :RegenerationScreen: sit on a panel in the palette's HUD panel colour at 80% opacity, their buttons outlined in its pulse-bar colour.

- During a :Run:, a control legend is drawn on the canvas at the bottom left of the :Level:, 16 px from its left and bottom edges, in 5 lines: `Swim: Up/Down or W/S`, `Turn: Left/Right or A/D`, `Sting: Space`, `Dash: Shift`, `Pause: P or Esc`.
  - Its text is Nunito 14 px, weight 400: each action label, up to and including the colon, in the palette's HUD text-secondary colour, and the keys after it in the HUD text colour.
  - It sits on a panel in the palette's HUD panel colour at 80% opacity.
  - Like :Hud:, it is drawn above the darkness and unshifted while a :Level: is dived into.
  - It is only drawn: nothing in the :Level: collides with it.
  - Nothing is placed under the control legend: no :GeneFragment:, :PlanktonCloud:, :Rift: or :Predator: is placed with any part of its circle inside the rectangle from `(0, 580)` to `(260, 720)`, as none is inside the rectangle :Hud: covers.
    - For a :StingingJelly: this holds for its bell and every tentacle segment; an :AnchovySchool:, placed off-screen, swims in as before.
    - Once placed, a :Predator: or a moving :GeneFragment: may move into the rectangle, as may the :Jellyfish:.
    - Every other placement rule still holds, and the same :RunSeed: still gives the same placements.

- Every page - :TitleScreen:, :DivePage: and the scoreboard page at `/scoreboard` - fills the browser window exactly, with no page margin and no scrollbar, in any window of at least 1024×600.
  - :DivePage: draws its canvas over the whole window; the 1280×720 :Level: is scaled to fit inside it and centred, as before, and the ocean continues into the bands around it.
    - The bands show the water gradient of the :Level:'s :Depth: band, running from the top of the window to its bottom, under the palette's darkness overlay wherever they lie outside the :Glow:, as the :Level: does.
    - While a :Level: is dived into, the bands take the same darkness overlay fading from fully opaque to clear, unshifted.
    - The bands are only drawn: the :Jellyfish: and every figure stay inside the :Level:, and :Hud: and the control legend keep their places in the :Level:.
    - No part of the window shows a plain black page background.
  - The scoreboard page with 10 rows, the :RunEnd: reason lines above them and its buttons fits in the window without scrolling, shrinking its table text if it must.

- :TitleScreen: shows a footer at the bottom of the page, `Powered by ***plain and turri · Source`, where `***plain` links to `https://plainlang.org/docs/`, `turri` to `https://github.com/turri-oss/turri`, and `Source` to `https://github.com/turri-oss/turritopsis-undying-tide`.
  - Each link opens in a new tab, with `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener"`.
  - Tab reaches the links after the :TitleScreen: buttons; Arrow Up and Arrow Down still move the focus between the buttons only.
  - The footer text is in the palette's HUD text-secondary colour, its links in the HUD text colour, underlined.
  - `***plain` is shown as written, with its three asterisks.
  - :TitleScreen: with the footer still fits in the window without scrolling.

- :TitleScreen: shows the goal of the game between its heading and its `Dive` button, in 3 lines: `Dive as deep as you can.`, `Collect every gene fragment to open the Rift to the next depth.` and `Be quick - the faster you reach each Rift, the higher your score.`
  - The first line is 22 px, weight 600, in the palette's HUD text colour; the other two are 16 px secondary text.
  - :TitleScreen: with the goal still fits in the window without scrolling.
  - The line beginning `Score:` that explains the score, on :RegenerationScreen: and the scoreboard page, is 14 px secondary text, at most 640 px wide, wrapping.

- :UpgradeChoice: sits on a panel in the palette's HUD panel colour at 80% opacity, over the :Level: under the palette's darkness overlay at 50% opacity, its texts set as on :PauseMenu:, `Depth <n> cleared` as secondary text.
  - Each button is a card 220 px wide with its :Upgrade: icon, 48 px, above its name, its level line in the HUD text-secondary colour, and its line of what it gives.
  - A card is outlined 1 px in the HUD text-secondary colour; the focused one 3 px in the pulse-bar colour and drawn 6 px higher.
  - The three cards and the panel fit in any window of at least 1024×600.

- :Hud: shows a row of the icons of the :Upgrade: kinds taken, 20 px each, below the hearts, in the order first taken.
  - Beside each icon but Stinging tentacles stands its level in Roman numerals, `I`, `II` or `III`, in the HUD text colour.
  - The row is not shown while no :Upgrade: is taken.
  - :Hud: stays within the rectangle from `(0, 0)` to `(300, 290)`, with 6 hearts and all seven kinds taken.

- With Stinging tentacles, each :Jellyfish: tentacle carries 5 barbs, short strokes 4 px long in the palette's sting colour, evenly spread from rim to tip, moving with the tentacle.
  - The barbs of a tentacle glint, brightening to full and back over 0.2 s once every 1 s, each tentacle at its own point of the cycle.
  - They are only drawn, and touch nothing.

- With Extra heart, the core of the :Jellyfish: figure is drawn 10% larger a level, about its own centre, inside a glow of radius 1.5 times the core's in the palette's heart colour at 30% opacity.
  - The :Jellyfish: circle stays radius 24.

- With Quick regeneration, a shimmer in the palette's plankton colour runs round the rim of the :Jellyfish: bell: an arc a quarter of the rim long, at 50% opacity, going round once every 2, 1.5 or 1 s at level 1, 2 or 3.
  - The halo of the polyp figure is drawn in the plankton colour in place of the player core colour, its opacity cycle unchanged.
  - The shimmer follows the bell's pulse.

- With Hard bell, the rim of the :Jellyfish: bell is drawn over as a stroke in the palette's bell-rim colour, 1, 2.5 or 4 px wide and at 50%, 70% or 90% opacity at level 1, 2 or 3, following the bell's pulse.
  - The :Jellyfish: circle stays radius 24.

- With Wide sting, a ring 1 px wide in the palette's sting colour at 10% opacity is drawn round the :Jellyfish: centre at the reach of the :Sting:, while the :Jellyfish: is not a :Polyp:.
  - It is drawn beneath every figure and above the water.

- With Fragment magnet, 1, 2 or 3 motes of radius 2 px in the palette's gene-fragment colour circle the :Jellyfish: centre 34 px out, once every 3 s, evenly spread, at level 1, 2 or 3.
  - A :GeneFragment: moving towards the :Jellyfish: leaves a trail of sparks of radius 1.5 px in the gene-fragment colour, one every 0.1 s where it was, each fading out over 0.3 s.
  - Motes and sparks are only drawn.

- When a :Level: starts after an :Upgrade: is taken, the :Jellyfish: figure flashes once: a disc of radius 32 in the palette's HUD text colour is drawn over it, fading from 70% opacity to clear over 0.4 s.

- With Longer tentacles, every :Jellyfish: tentacle is drawn 1.25, 1.5 or 1.75 times its length at level 1, 2 or 3.
  - Its sway at the tip and its tip's draw towards the bell's centre line grow by the same factor; its sway timing, lag and taper from 3 px to 1 px stay as they are.
  - With Stinging tentacles too, its 5 barbs stay evenly spread from rim to the new tip.
  - The tentacles are only drawn, and touch nothing.
